WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:12.560
In recent years, open access has steadily gained&nbsp;
momentum. Most journals and publishers today have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:18.400
open access channels and authors have the choice&nbsp;
to publish open access. However, many authors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:23.200
particularly those who are relatively new&nbsp;
to academia, are still in a haze about open&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:29.840
access publishing. What is open access? What&nbsp;
is the rationale behind publishing open access?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:36.800
What are the different venues for publishing open&nbsp;
access? Such questions bother authors and they are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:43.840
often skeptical about publishing open access&nbsp;
as there are several myths about open access.&nbsp;

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:49.120
Open access is built upon the idea that&nbsp;
scientific research should be made freely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:53.760
available to all so that others can build&nbsp;
upon it and help escalate scientific progress.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:59.120
Traditionally, the academic publishing industry&nbsp;
has followed a subscription-based model.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:03.440
This model requires readers to pay&nbsp;
for the content that they read.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:09.680
Typically, libraries purchase bulk subscription&nbsp;
to a journal so that members or students can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:14.800
access the journals. But as subscription&nbsp;
charges for journals started increasing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:18.560
libraries found it increasingly&nbsp;
difficult to purchase expensive journals.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:24.080
This was particularly true for libraries and&nbsp;
institutions in developing countries where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:30.400
funding was scarce. As a result, researchers often&nbsp;
could not access studies that they wished to,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:34.880
and this started affecting the progress&nbsp;
of research. The need to remove this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:39.760
roadblock gave rise to the open access model of&nbsp;
publishing in which readers have unrestricted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:44.240
and immediate access to research after it has&nbsp;
been published with the permission to reuse it.&nbsp;

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:48.560
What are the different venues&nbsp;
for publishing open access? 
 &nbsp;

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:56.160
Broadly speaking, there are two models for&nbsp;
open access publishing : gold and green .
 &nbsp;

00:01:56.160 --> 00:02:01.520
Gold open access journals give readers free access&nbsp;
to peer reviewed articles, but the publication&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:07.920
charges are borne by the authors. Today, most big&nbsp;
publishers offer open access options, and some,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:14.400
like plause, are purely open access. There are&nbsp;
several major directories of open access journals,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:20.240
most notably Directory of Open Access Journals,&nbsp;
or DOAJ, which can help researchers identify&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:25.920
open access journals in their field. Under the&nbsp;
gold open access model, authors have different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:31.040
kinds of journals to choose from :
 
Full open access journals . All&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:35.840
articles published in such journals are freely&nbsp;
available for readers on the journal website.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:41.120
Some of these journals are subsidized,&nbsp;
and financed by an academic institution,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:45.840
a learned society, or by the government; but&nbsp;
others may require the payment of a fee from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:50.800
authors, known as article processing charges,&nbsp;
once the paper is accepted for publication.
 &nbsp;

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:56.160
Hybrid journals . Most of the articles&nbsp;
in these journals are paywalled,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.160 --> 00:03:01.200
with only some content open. Authors can&nbsp;
choose to provide open access to their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:06.560
articles by paying an extra fee. This fee&nbsp;
is generally known as open access fee. 
 &nbsp;

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:13.520
Delayed open access journals . In this model,&nbsp;
articles become free for readers some time after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:19.600
initial publication. The time period for which the&nbsp;
article is paywalled is known as embargo period.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:26.080
For most journals, the embargo period is&nbsp;
six to twelve months. [sPause sec=1 ePause]
 &nbsp;

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:32.160
Green open access . Under green open access,&nbsp;
authors publish in subscription-based journals,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:36.240
but at the same time deposit their&nbsp;
articles in an open access repository.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:42.400
This is known as self-archiving. Thus,&nbsp;
although the journal is behind a paywall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:47.440
readers have free access to the article&nbsp;
through the repository. Authors who cannot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:52.720
pay the fees for publishing in open access&nbsp;
journals often take this route. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:59.200
articles may not be peer reviewed prior to posting&nbsp;
in a repository. Another point to be kept in mind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:04.000
is that not all subscription-based journals allow&nbsp;
authors to post their paper on a repository.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:09.120
Authors should, therefore, check the website&nbsp;
of their target journal to find out whether&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:13.840
self-archiving is allowed, and preferably take&nbsp;
the journal’s permission before self-archiving.&nbsp;

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:23.520
Open access repositories can be institutional or&nbsp;
independent, subject-specific, such as bioRxiv,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:27.840
Nature Precedings, and PubMed Central,&nbsp;
or multidisciplinary such as arXiv.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:34.240
There are three basic versions of an article&nbsp;
that can be self-archived in repositories :
 &nbsp;

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:40.640
Pre-Prints : This refers to the author’s copy of&nbsp;
the article before it has been peer reviewed .
 &nbsp;

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:44.480
Post-Prints : This also&nbsp;
refers to the author’s copy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:49.200
but after it has been peer reviewed, with the&nbsp;
suggested revisions incorporated, but before the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:55.200
publisher has formatted it for publication .
 
and, Publisher’s version :: This refers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:59.920
to the final PDF of the article that is&nbsp;
formatted and appears in print or online.&nbsp;

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:07.600
As mentioned at the outset, authors are&nbsp;
often unsure about publishing open access.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:13.040
This is largely due to some popular&nbsp;
misconceptions about open access in their minds.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:20.160
Let us try to dispel some of these myths :
 
Open access journals are not peer reviewed :&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:22.240
This is an absolutely wrong idea.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:27.120
A journal’s peer review policy has&nbsp;
nothing to do with its access policy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:34.880
Most open access journals are peer-reviewed .
 
Open access journals have low impact factors :&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:40.400
This is, once again, a myth. Many open&nbsp;
access journals publish highly cited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:47.360
articles and receive high impact factors . 
 
Publishing in open access journals is expensive :&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:51.920
Authors often avoid publishing in open access&nbsp;
journals as they feel that they will not be able&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:58.800
to afford the high APCs. However, the truth is&nbsp;
that not all open access journals charge APCs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:02.800
and the ones that do generally have the&nbsp;
APCs clearly mentioned on their website.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:10.880
APCs vary across journals and are not always high.&nbsp;
Additionally, many universities or funding bodies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:17.840
bear the APCs. Also, open access journals often&nbsp;
waive fees for researchers in developing countries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:23.840
and those researchers who are in financial&nbsp;
difficulty. For example, many Nature Publishing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:30.080
Group journals have an APC waiver policy .
 
Open access publishing does not offer copyright&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:37.120
protection or credit to authors : In fact, for&nbsp;
many open access journals, such as PLOS or BMJ,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:43.040
authors retain copyright after publication.&nbsp;
Additionally, most open access journals use&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:47.840
Creative Commons licenses under which authors&nbsp;
always receive credit when their work is reused.
 &nbsp;

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:56.320
In summary , As an early-career researcher,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.320 --> 00:07:02.000
it is extremely important for you to recognize&nbsp;
the importance of publishing open access.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:06.800
Science can progress only when immediate,&nbsp;
unrestricted access to research is provided.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:12.880
We hope that in the coming years, researchers show&nbsp;
more willingness to publish open access so that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:20.960
the scientific community, policy makers, and the&nbsp;
general public can benefit from their research.

